# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# The supervisor reads its stand-in counts before any child runs, and
# they are below both limits, so every child runs; when faulter faults, the
# supervisor reports the counts the next boot would hold and resets the
# board. The read-only stand-in stores nothing, so the next boot reads the
# same counts. The "fault detail" and "had run" lines are not checked.
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children faulter (0) and trigger (1)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: counts read from the test stand-in, which stores nothing: restart count 1, sensitive count 0
NOWAYOS: supervisor: this start: a reset whose cause was not written down
NOWAYOS: supervisor: restart count 2 of 4, sensitive count 0 of 2: restart, counted
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter: no marker - this boot's memory is fresh
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter wrote its marker; waiting for the trigger
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: trigger notifying faulter
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter triggered
NOWAYOS: supervisor: faulter stopped: data write at 0x40001000: permission fault (the mapping does not allow it)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: the next boot would hold restart count 3 of 4, sensitive count 1 of 2: restart, counted
NOWAYOS: supervisor: resetting the board
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children faulter (0) and trigger (1)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: counts read from the test stand-in, which stores nothing: restart count 1, sensitive count 0
NOWAYOS: supervisor: restart count 2 of 4, sensitive count 0 of 2: restart, counted
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter: no marker - this boot's memory is fresh

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# the fail-safe state, the marker surviving the reset, the reset returning, a
# fault the monitor had to handle, a kernel error message, or the supervisor
# or a probe failing.
!fail-safe
!SURVIVED
!the reset returned
!NOT stopped
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!ISOLATION FAILURE
!no probe is defined
!no children are defined
!cannot
